  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195500: Bounded PostgreSQL startup metadata state machine

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The Kotoba PostgreSQL provider no longer assumes a fixed 15-byte
AuthenticationOk plus ReadyForQuery response. It reads at most 4,096 bytes and
admits one AuthenticationOk followed by bounded ParameterStatus and
BackendKeyData messages and one final ReadyForQuery. ParameterStatus must
contain exactly two non-empty NUL-terminated fields. BackendKeyData must have
the protocol-defined 13-byte frame size.

Malformed lengths, unknown tags, ErrorResponse, authentication repetition,
metadata before AuthenticationOk, data after ReadyForQuery and buffer
exhaustion fail closed and close the channel.

## Maturity boundary

This establishes the no-password startup metadata state machine. SCRAM-SHA-256,
secret custody, server-final verification, cancellation and production
PostgreSQL interoperability remain separate qualification gates.")))
